GIMP Palette
Name: MonoGame.GameFramework
Columns: 7
#
# The canonical palette for every sprite in this repo. Aseprite reads and
# writes .gpl natively (Palette menu -> Load Palette), so this file is both
# the authoring artifact and the thing CI enforces -- there is no second copy
# to drift from.
#
# Derived 2026-08-11 from the 14 colours actually in use across the Platformer
# hero's four frames. It is deliberately the *observed* palette, not an
# idealised one: a gate that fails on day one against committed art teaches
# people to ignore the gate.
#
# Organised as ramps. Each ramp is one material, ordered dark -> light, and a
# sprite should draw its shading from within a single ramp. Light comes from
# the top-left (see STYLE.md), so the dark end of a ramp lives on the
# bottom-right of a form.
#
# RESOLVED 2026-08-12: this palette used to carry a second blue at the same
# ramp slot, #3A5FA0 "blue-2-mid-alt" -- 4 degrees of hue from #2A5DA0 and
# identical in value. One pixel of each appeared in every hero frame, which is
# the signature of a stray colour-picker nudge rather than a decision.
#
# #2A5DA0 won on ramp fit, not on usage (both were used exactly once per file).
# Going up this ramp hue trends 217.1 -> 211.9 and saturation 73.0 -> 69.5;
# #2A5DA0 sits inside both trends at H214.1/S73.8, while #3A5FA0 broke both
# (H218.2 moved the wrong way, S63.8 fell 10 points below the slot). The stray
# pixels were repainted by running conform-sprite against this file -- the
# pipeline fixing its own input.
#
